<title>USA: Rep. Archer to battle U.S. ethanol tax subsidy.</title>
<headline>Rep. Archer to battle U.S. ethanol tax subsidy.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The chairman of the powerful House Ways and Means Committee will form a bipartisan congressional coalition dedicated to taking action this year against federal ethanol subsidies.</p>
<p>In a news release, Texas Republican Rep. Bill Archer also said he would hold a news conference Thursday to release a General Accounting Office study on the ethanol tax subsidy.</p>
<p>Archer made an unsuccessful effort to attack federal tax breaks for ethanol during the last session of Congress.</p>
<p>The tax preference was saved by House Speaker Newt Gingrich.</p>
</text>
